[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Not for Jazz]
[00:14.59]What happened to the clavichord?
[00:20.26]We have an old musical instrument.
[00:24.48]It is called a clavichord.
[00:28.49]It was made in Germany in 1681.
[00:33.10]Our clavichord is kept in the living room.
[00:36.76]It has belonged to our family for a long time.
[00:41.47]The instrument was bought by my grandfather many years ago.
[00:47.54]Recently it was damaged by a visitor.
[00:51.45]She tried to play jazz on it!
[00:55.13]She struck the keys too hard and two of the strings were broken.
[01:02.23]My father was shocked.
[01:05.42]Now we are not allowed to touch it.
[01:08.28]It is being repaired by a friend of my father's.
